Hi Igor,

SIZE_E_1 stays at 0 and the diff stays as it is. Your reason is better than the
one I would have given: a register built from the trace with one field swapped
to upstream's value is a configuration nothing has ever run, and that is worth
more than a smaller diff.

Your question has an answer and it is partly uncomfortable, so let me give the
measurement rather than the summary. Since we last spoke I swept SIZE_E_2 across
all eight of its values on a second path, the int4 one, at 64 output channels:

    SIZE_E_2       0    1    2    3    4..7
    words written  32   32   36   40   the job hangs

and the count that came out CORRECT stayed at 32 in all of them, so what the
field moves is how many words the block writes, not how many channels it
computes.

So on that path the field is additive in FOURS, not in sixteens. That does not
sit well with the semantics I sent you on the 17th, where SIZE_E_n + 1 counted
16-channel atoms. It is a different register value on a different precision, so
it does not refute the reading for the path it was read from, and I am not going
to pretend it supports it either.

SIZE_E_1 on that path is inert: setting it from 1 to 0 leaves the channel count
at 40 and the probe's sixteen point window unchanged. That is a smaller claim
than "no effect" and it is the size of what I actually read. SIZE_E_0 is inert at
0 and hangs at 2 and at 6. RGP_CNTER and OD_BYPASS are inert, RESERVED_0 hangs.

Now the part your question actually asks. I said I would cross the two and I
have, at seven channel counts, with the control alongside each one in the same
boot rather than borrowed from an earlier round:

    N                     16   24   32   40   48   56   64
    SIZE_E_1 = 1  wrote   16   24   32   40   48   56   64
                  correct 16   24   32   40   48   56   64
    SIZE_E_1 = 0  wrote    8   24   32   40   48   56   64
                  correct  8   24   32   40   48   56   64

Six of the seven are identical, so SIZE_E_1 is inert at 24, 32, 40, 48, 56 and
64 and I can say that with a control under it now rather than as an impression.

At N = 16 it is not inert. Asking for sixteen channels with the field at
upstream's 0 delivers eight, and both the words written and the count that comes
out correct halve. One shape in seven, the smallest one, and it is exactly the
kind of thing two shapes could not have found. So your conservative choice is
not just tidier, it is right, and I would not have known that without the sweep
you asked for.

I also owe you a correction on the way to this. The first version of this reply
said I had not run the cross sweep and I had; the round is titled after you. And
it was half a round, because it swept SIZE_E_1 = 0 at all seven N and never ran
the traced value beside them, so four of the seven only had a control by accident
elsewhere in the log. The table above is the round that fixes that.

And the loose end I was going to hand you is closed by the same run. I had an
earlier measurement that asking for n channels writes floor(n/16)*16 of them,
and I was about to tell you that SIZE_E_1 = 0 might be what lifts it. It is not:
in this round the traced value writes all 24 at N = 24 too. That earlier
shortfall belongs to a different setting of the channel count register, not to
this field, and comparing across two rounds is what made it look otherwise.

The re-run offer is noted and I will take it when v9 goes. Glad the trip was
fine, and I hope the countryside is treating the board well.

Regards,
Jiaxing
